VeridianOS: FindIconv names its results after the package

cmake/FindIconv.cmake (used by find_package(Iconv)) passed "ICONV" to
find_package_handle_standard_args(), which CMake reports ("The package
name passed to find_package_handle_standard_args() (ICONV) does not match
the name of the calling package (Iconv)"). It now passes "Iconv";
find_package_handle_standard_args() sets ICONV_FOUND as well as
Iconv_FOUND, so the module's own checks and CMakeLists.txt's summary,
which read ICONV_FOUND, see the same result.

--- a/cmake/FindIconv.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindIconv.cmake
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
 # handle the QUIETLY and REQUIRED arguments and set ICONV_FOUND to TRUE if
 # all listed variables are TRUE
 include(FindPackageHandleStandardArgs)
-find_package_handle_standard_args(ICONV
+find_package_handle_standard_args(Iconv
     REQUIRED_VARS ICONV_FOUND_ANY ICONV_INCLUDE_DIR
     VERSION_VAR ICONV_VERSION_STRING)
 
